# nextflow-head.vars.example — the Nomad Variable the head job reads for secrets.
#
# On YOUR Nomad cluster, before `nomad job run nextflow-head.nomad.hcl`, create a
# Nomad Variable at path `nomad/jobs/nextflow-head` with these keys. Nothing
# secret is baked into the job spec; it is fetched at runtime from this Variable.
#
#   nomad var put nomad/jobs/nextflow-head \
#     nomad_token=<ACL token the Nextflow executor uses to submit process jobs> \
#     s3_access_key=<S3 access key for the work-dir bucket, E2 only> \
#     s3_secret_key=<S3 secret key, E2 only>
#
# For E1 (host-volume POSIX work dir) the s3_* keys are unused but harmless.
# Give the token an ACL policy allowing job submit/read in the target namespace.
